# Data-Aware Monitoring: Understanding the "Why"
Traditional monitoring answers: "Did the task run?" Data-aware monitoring answers: "Did the data arrive correctly, on time, and with the right quality to support business decisions?" This is the critical distinction Astro Observe makes.
- Quality Beyond Status
Monitors evaluate data quality and business impact, not just task execution state
- Proactive Failure Monitor
Automatically alerts when any upstream or final DAG in a data product fails, before downstream consumers are affected
- Lineage-Linked Alerts
Every alert links directly to the lineage view, enabling instant identification of impacted assets and root cause navigation
When alert occurs:
    Alert
    ↓
    Failing Asset
    ↓
    Lineage Graph
    ↓
    Root Cause
No need to manually investigate for hours

# Monitors in Astro Observe: Proactive Problem Solving
Monitors are the operational heart of Astro Observe. They run continuously, evaluate pipeline and data product health against defined policies, and take action the moment something deviates from expected behavior.

How Monitors Work
- Continuously assess data product and pipeline health against defined criteria
- Evaluate SLA adherence on every pipeline run 
- Detect failures in upstream dependencies before they surface downstream

Alert Severity Levels
